      "text": "**I’d skip the outdoor jog right now.** Around **4:45 p.m. in Penang on October 17**, George Town’s latest reading was **71 on the US AQI scale (“moderate”)**—not generally too polluted for a healthy adult to jog, though people unusually sensitive to particle pollution should keep exercise shorter and easier. That reading is for George Town, so check a station closer to you if you’re elsewhere in Penang. ([iqair.com](https://www.iqair.com/air-quality/malaysia/penang/george-town))\n\nThe more immediate issue is **thunderstorms**: the current George Town weather report shows a thundershower. Wait until the storm passes and **30 minutes after the last thunder** before running outside. ([weather.gov](https://www.weather.gov/mlb/lightning_rules?utm_source=openai))",
